  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is given by $\u27e8x,y\u27e9=6{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+6{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ Find $\u27e8x,y\u27e9$, if\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8x,y\u27e9 & =6{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+6{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =6\\cdot 1\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =12+18-8 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
